    "body": "Bumps the github-actions group with 3 updates in the / directory: [korthout/backport-action](https://github.com/korthout/backport-action), [vmactions/openbsd-vm](https://github.com/vmactions/openbsd-vm) and [msys2/setup-msys2](https://github.com/msys2/setup-msys2).\n\nUpdates `korthout/backport-action` from 4.6.1 to 4.7.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/releases\">korthout/backport-action's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>Backport-action v4.7.0</h2>\n<h2>What's Changed</h2>\n<p>Thanks to a great contribution by <a href=\"https://github.com/lexfrei\"><code>@​lexfrei</code></a>, backports no longer fail when the target branch already contains some of the changes, for example if a specific commit was already manually cherry-picked, or on a re-run. Previously, git reported the empty cherry-pick as a conflict, so the backport failed (or opened a draft PR with <code>conflict_resolution: draft_commit_conflicts</code>).</p>\n<p>Now the action skips those commits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Some commits already on the target:</strong> the backport PR is created as usual. The comment on the original pull request mentions the skipped commits, and a comment on the backport PR lists them.</li>\n<li><strong>All commits already on the target:</strong> there's nothing to backport, so no PR is created. The target is skipped, just like when its backport PR already exists, and doesn't count as a failure in <code>was_successful</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>With <code>comment_style: summary</code>, that looks like this:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Target</th>\n<th>Status</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>stable/8.7</code></td>\n<td>:white_check_mark: Created <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/korthout/backport-action/issues/612\">#612</a> — 1 commit skipped (target already contains changes)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>stable/8.6</code></td>\n<td>:heavy_minus_sign: Skipped (target already contains changes)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</blockquote>\n<p>No configuration needed to enable this. This is a bug fix released in a new minor version to avoid surprising users with new behavior.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Skip commits the target branch already contains by <a href=\"https://github.com/lexfrei\"><code>@​lexfrei</code></a> in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/korthout/backport-action/pull/705\">korthout/backport-action#705</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>New Contributors</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/lexfrei\"><code>@​lexfrei</code></a> made their first contribution in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/korthout/backport-action/pull/705\">korthout/backport-action#705</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Updated dependencies</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update korthout/backport-action action to v4.6.1 by <a href=\"https://github.com/renovate\"><code>@​renovate</code></a>[bot] in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/korthout/backport-action/pull/718\">korthout/backport-action#718</a></li>\n<li>Update dependency prettier to v3.9.9 by <a href=\"https://github.com/renovate\"><code>@​renovate</code></a>[bot] in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/korthout/backport-action/pull/720\">korthout/backport-action#720</a></li>\n<li>Lock file maintenance by <a href=\"https://github.com/renovate\"><code>@​renovate</code></a>[bot] in <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/korthout/backport-action/pull/721\">korthout/backport-action#721</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Full Changelog</strong>: <a href=\"https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/compare/v4.6.1...v4.7.0\">https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/compare/v4.6.1...v4.7.0</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/commit/8560fb503c275d433c56f05a2f64850093baa9f7\"><code>8560fb5</code></a> dist: release 4.7.0</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/commit/ed61f3ea25edc33b6754e20b6c4f57006969e1f6\"><code>ed61f3e</code></a> dist: build new artifacts</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/commit/ab5a1f2a39c245a62e40d2e86b4b2301a5c6bd2f\"><code>ab5a1f2</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/korthout/backport-action/issues/721\">#721</a> from korthout/renovate/lock-file-maintenance</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/commit/589f023502874231aaf8b003fdcfea6c3a1e7e5e\"><code>589f023</code></a> Lock file maintenance</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/commit/0bf77c70e9039c38f47a62f51982e74889af1bc3\"><code>0bf77c7</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/korthout/backport-action/issues/720\">#720</a> from korthout/renovate/prettier-3.x</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/commit/07bacb35a2baf42f915a729df36d309e954aa336\"><code>07bacb3</code></a> Update dependency prettier to v3.9.9</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/commit/04a4bac6305d7ced7ae11f6f58020729c6fca175\"><code>04a4bac</code></a> dist: build new artifacts</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/commit/09d3c41ab439c68e1e09052ab8d8fc9155126aaa\"><code>09d3c41</code></a> Merge pull request <a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/korthout/backport-action/issues/705\">#705</a> from lexfrei/fix/empty-cherry-pick</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/commit/15cff3767215191cbdf3b36f3ecfe4ec1dbea952\"><code>15cff37</code></a> Add skipped commit to the glossary</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/commit/54c8afc92c80ac90b978546acbd3556992eb7ec3\"><code>54c8afc</code></a> Reword the skipped-commits comment on the backport PR</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/korthout/backport-action/compare/6b65649031ac6d18ffdfd0c0820e9436f3fde22b...8560fb503c275d433c56f05a2f64850093baa9f7\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `vmactions/openbsd-vm` from 1.4.7 to 1.4.8\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/vmactions/openbsd-vm/releases\">vmactions/openbsd-vm's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v1.4.8</h2>\n<p>OpenBSD on ubuntu-26.04 runners</p>\n<p>The action's test matrix now runs on ubuntu-26.04 and ubuntu-26.04-arm:\n113 of 114 jobs pass, and the 9p job is skipped as before.</p>\n<h2>What failed on 26.04</h2>\n<p>With v1.4.7 on a 26.04 runner:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Every riscv64 job stopped at</p>\n<p>Error: QEMU binary 'qemu-system-riscv64' not found (searched PATH\nand common install locations).</p>\n<p>Since Ubuntu 25.10 the riscv64 emulator ships in a separate\nqemu-system-riscv package, no longer in qemu-system-misc.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>x86_64, aarch64 and sparc64 were not affected.</p>\n<h2>Fixes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The action installs qemu-system-riscv instead of qemu-system-misc\nfor riscv64 on Ubuntu releases newer than 24.04.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The package fix engages only on Ubuntu releases newer than 24.04, so\njobs on ubuntu-24.04 run as before. The rest of anyvm 0.7.2's 26.04\nwork:\n<a href=\"https://github.com/anyvm-org/anyvm/releases/tag/v0.7.2\">https://github.com/anyvm-org/anyvm/releases/tag/v0.7.2</a></p>\n<h2>Fixed: a lost network probe no longer fails as &quot;Unsupported OS&quot;</h2>\n<p><a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/vmactions/freebsd-vm/issues/163\">vmactions/freebsd-vm#163</a>: a job failed after three minutes with</p>\n<p>Error: Unsupported OS: freebsd. Builder repository\nanyvm-org/freebsd-builder not found.</p>\n<p>although the image exists. A single failed probe of the release download\nURL sent the run down the GitHub REST API. The action never passed a\ntoken, so that request was unauthenticated and shared the 60/hour per-IP\nlimit with every other job on the runner IP; the 403 was retried for\nthree minutes and then reported as an unsupported OS. This action took\nthe same path. Two changes close it:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>New input: token. It defaults to github.token and is handed to the\nVM runtime, so the release lookup is authenticated (1000 requests\nper hour per repository instead of 60 shared). Nothing to change in</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vmactions/openbsd-vm/commit/5f7b2c933b8846a138361d6843c52af4bef5d945\"><code>5f7b2c9</code></a> Update vmactions/openbsd-vm from base-vm</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vmactions/openbsd-vm/commit/5119f71611d14be5ecad0dcadb60b0d61daeaff6\"><code>5119f71</code></a> Generated from base-vm</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vmactions/openbsd-vm/commit/d22f98edac371e6c61678b2ca91a6d065bae5932\"><code>d22f98e</code></a> Bump versions from upstream releases</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vmactions/openbsd-vm/commit/37423ccea3e2f711efbdc49cc510296227a89721\"><code>37423cc</code></a> Update vmactions/openbsd-vm from base-vm</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vmactions/openbsd-vm/commit/ced39895ab57b046650dcd3a7fc8a876afaeaadc\"><code>ced3989</code></a> Generated from base-vm</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vmactions/openbsd-vm/commit/5ca77d9b743cbe4e48a2e1655dfb103ba537c608\"><code>5ca77d9</code></a> Update vmactions/openbsd-vm from base-vm</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vmactions/openbsd-vm/commit/01dd7969fe344899da14010843ca926c634958fa\"><code>01dd796</code></a> Generated from base-vm</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vmactions/openbsd-vm/commit/104bc8f5b82c4c900affbe2726aa2c67d221bd82\"><code>104bc8f</code></a> Bump versions from upstream releases</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vmactions/openbsd-vm/commit/8ae27e66e2c2b0bcf122be0c36afadc87bbfca60\"><code>8ae27e6</code></a> Update vmactions/openbsd-vm from base-vm</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/vmactions/openbsd-vm/commit/c4397655a179641400c6ae2f2e660cd1c702d8bc\"><code>c439765</code></a> Generated from base-vm</li>\n<li>Additional commits viewable in <a href=\"https://github.com/vmactions/openbsd-vm/compare/86cdc08415d9d0865267e686561e276c52d62530...5f7b2c933b8846a138361d6843c52af4bef5d945\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\nUpdates `msys2/setup-msys2` from 2.32.0 to 2.33.0\n<details>\n<summary>Release notes</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/releases\">msys2/setup-msys2's releases</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h2>v2.33.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update base distribution to <a href=\"https://github.com/msys2/msys2-installer/releases/tag/2026-09-27\">20260927</a>. [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/pull/657\">#657</a>]</li>\n<li>Due to dependency cleanups &quot;perl&quot; and some related libraries are no longer installed by default.</li>\n<li>Add a deprecation warning for MINGW32/MINGW64. See the new <code>suppress-deprecation-warnings</code> option for how to silence them. [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/pull/644\">#644</a>]</li>\n<li>pacboy caching fixes [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/pull/650\">#650</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependencies</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Changelog</summary>\n<p><em>Sourced from <a href=\"https://github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\">msys2/setup-msys2's changelog</a>.</em></p>\n<blockquote>\n<h1>Changelog</h1>\n<h2>2.33.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update base distribution to <a href=\"https://github.com/msys2/msys2-installer/releases/tag/2026-09-27\">20260927</a>. [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/pull/657\">#657</a>]</li>\n<li>Due to dependency cleanups &quot;perl&quot; and some related libraries are no longer installed by default.</li>\n<li>Add a deprecation warning for MINGW32/MINGW64. See the new <code>suppress-deprecation-warnings</code> option for how to silence them. [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/pull/644\">#644</a>]</li>\n<li>pacboy caching fixes [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/pull/650\">#650</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependencies</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.32.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update base distribution to <a href=\"https://github.com/msys2/msys2-installer/releases/tag/2026-06-11\">20260611</a>. [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/pull/624\">#624</a>]</li>\n<li>Port from ncc to rolldown for bundling</li>\n<li>Include an SBOM of the bundle</li>\n<li>Update dependencies</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.31.1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>input: allow empty input for &quot;install&quot; and &quot;pacboy&quot;, meaning not packages will\nbe installed [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/issues/589\">#589</a>]</li>\n<li>input: deprecate the special &quot;RUNNER_TEMP&quot; value for &quot;location&quot; in favor of an\nempty string</li>\n<li>Update dependencies</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.31.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update base distribution to <a href=\"https://github.com/msys2/msys2-installer/releases/tag/2026-03-22\">20260322</a>. [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/pull/597\">#597</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependencies</li>\n<li>Move to node24 from node20</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.30.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update base distribution to <a href=\"https://github.com/msys2/msys2-installer/releases/tag/2025-12-13\">20251213</a>. [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/pull/565\">#565</a>]</li>\n<li>Remove folder-hash dependency [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/pull/555\">#555</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependencies</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.29.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Allow installation to C:\\msys64 if it doesn't exist already. Like with the new <code>windows-11-arm</code> image, for example. [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/issues/542\">#542</a>]</li>\n<li>Update base distribution to <a href=\"https://github.com/msys2/msys2-installer/releases/tag/2025-08-30\">20250830</a>. [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/pull/548\">#548</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependencies</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.28.0</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Update base distribution to <a href=\"https://github.com/msys2/msys2-installer/releases/tag/2025-06-22\">20250622</a>. [<a href=\"https://redirect.github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/pull/518\">#518</a>]</li>\n<li>Update dependencies</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>2.27.0</h2>\n<!-- raw HTML omitted -->\n</blockquote>\n<p>... (truncated)</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>Commits</summary>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/commit/ec48f7c5447b3140e2b088413ae3a55687bccb6e\"><code>ec48f7c</code></a> v2.33.0 d34ca6fb9f66412423e0ade249ca8a35b3715726</li>\n<li>See full diff in <a href=\"https://github.com/msys2/setup-msys2/compare/66cd2cce69caa17b53920067426061ca1de3a884...ec48f7c5447b3140e2b088413ae3a55687bccb6e\">compare view</a></li>\n</ul>\n</details>\n<br />\n\n\nDependabot will resolve any conflicts with this PR as long as you don't alter it yourself. You can also trigger a rebase manually by commenting `@dependabot rebase`.\n\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-start)\n[//]: # (dependabot-automerge-end)\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>Dependabot commands and options</summary>\n<br />\n\nYou can trigger Dependabot actions by commenting on this PR:\n- `@dependabot rebase` will rebase this PR\n- `@dependabot recreate` will recreate this PR, overwriting any edits that have been made to it\n- `@dependabot show <dependency name> ignore conditions` will show all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> major version` will close this group update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency's major version (unless you unignore this specific dependency's major version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name> minor version` will close this group update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency's minor version (unless you unignore this specific dependency's minor version or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot ignore <dependency name>` will close this group update PR and stop Dependabot creating any more for the specific dependency (unless you unignore this specific dependency or upgrade to it yourself)\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name>` will remove all of the ignore conditions of the specified dependency\n- `@dependabot unignore <dependency name> <ignore condition>` will remove the ignore condition of the specified dependency and ignore conditions\n\n\n</details>",
